# RestPilot project rules

- Application **source code** must be in **English** (identifiers, comments, internal docs in code).
- User-facing text uses **i18n** only: English (default) and Spanish (neutral formal). Update `src/i18n/en.ts` and `src/i18n/es.ts` together.
- **Persistence**: `config.json` via Tauri (`load_app_config`/`save_app_config`); response history (`lastResponse`/`lastError`/`savedResponses`) lives separately in `responses.json` (`load_response_cache`/`save_response_cache`). Never use `localStorage` / `sessionStorage`. No fallback compatibility for removed storage. See **AGENTS.md → Persistence**.
- **Clear all data**: new `UserSettings` / `AppConfig` fields → `defaultSettings()` / `defaultConfig()`; new `AppState` runtime fields → `defaultRuntimeState()` in `src/app/reset-app-state.ts`. See **AGENTS.md → Clear all data**.
- **Themes**: preserve existing light styling; extend dark via `[data-theme="dark"]`. Use `--rp-*` tokens (remapped in dark); do not replace the design system unless asked. **Never write a colour literal** — in CSS, React inline styles or injected HTML. Translucent tints use `rgb(var(--rp-<family>-rgb) / <alpha>)`. Main components stay on five hue families (neutral, accent, danger, warning, success); `--http-method-*` and syntax colours are the only exceptions. See **AGENTS.md → UI and theming**.
- **Headers are ordered `[name, value]` pairs, never a map/object** — a `HashMap`/`Record` silently drops repeated header names (`Set-Cookie`, duplicate `Accept`, etc). See **AGENTS.md → HTTP → Headers and response body**.
- **Response bodies can be base64** (`body_is_base64`); use `body_size` for displayed sizes, never `body.length`. Same section as above.
- **Dialogs**: the UI is React (`src/react/`) for anything new; the imperative `applicationDialog`/`messageDialog` system (`src/components/dialogs.ts` + `AppDialog.tsx`) still powers historical modes (import, export, proxy test log, settings). Extending an existing mode touches `DialogMode`, `captureDialogForm`, `bindDialogPreviewContent`, and `AppDialog.tsx`'s `bodyClassName` — see **AGENTS.md → Dialogs** for the full checklist before adding one.
- **Popovers**: use `renderPopoverShell()` in `src/components/popover.ts`; every popover must have a top-right close button (`data-popover-close`).
- **Settings**: `AppConfig.settings` holds theme, language, and proxy. Settings UI lives in `src/react/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`.
- **Import**: adding a new import source (beyond RestPilot/Postman/OpenAPI/cURL) means a new `ImportSource` value, a `parseXxx()` producing `ImportParseResult`, a detection branch in `src/import/detect.ts`, and i18n `importSourceXxx`/`importSourceXxxDesc` labels. See **AGENTS.md → Import**.
- Keep changes focused; match existing patterns in `src/styles.css` and the relevant `src/app/`, `src/react/`, or `src/import/` module.
- **New tabs / panels / sections**: follow **AGENTS.md → “Flex and panel layout”**, **“Panel insets”**, and **“Field remove control”** (`mini-btn field-remove-btn` for × deletes). Copy `params`, `headers`, or `auth` markup/CSS; do not ship until resize looks correct.
- **Settings toggles**: checkbox rows use `.settings-toggle-row` (`auto auto`, `fit-content`). Do not put toggles in a grid column with `1fr` beside them.
